#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""magician kg-mcp — read-only MCP server over the local knowledge-graph index (stdio, stdlib only).

Serves the index that `kg init` builds to any MCP client, such as Claude Code, Codex or the ChatGPT
desktop app. It is opt-in: magician does not register it. See
skills/knowledge-graph/references/mcp-server.md for the `claude mcp add` and `.mcp.json` snippets.

Usage:
  kg-mcp [--repo DIR]      serve MCP over stdin/stdout (newline-delimited JSON-RPC 2.0)
  kg-mcp --version
  kg-mcp -h | --help

Repository: --repo DIR, else $CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR, else the current folder. The index location is
the one `kg` uses (${MAGICIAN_HOME:-$HOME/.claude/magician}/knowledge-graph/).

Protocol: dual-era. A request whose params._meta holds io.modelcontextprotocol/protocolVersion gets
stateless 2026-07-28 behaviour (server/discover, resultType, per-request version check). Any other
request gets legacy behaviour (initialize, notifications/initialized, ping), for 2025-11-25 and
earlier clients. Tools: kg_query, kg_blast, kg_neighbors, kg_status. No resources, prompts, roots,
sampling or logging.

Guarantees: no network; never writes the repository or the index. The graph DB is opened with
SQLite `mode=ro` and `PRAGMA query_only`. SQLite can create its `-wal`/`-shm` side files next to
graph.db when they are missing, as `kg` itself does. Paging state is in an opaque cursor that the
client sends back, never in server memory. Diagnostics go to stderr only.
"""
import base64
import json
